# Branching (protected `main` and `development`)

`main` and `development` are **protected**. Never commit, push, merge, or rebase onto them directly. Never force-push them.

```text
feature/<name>  →  development  →  main
```

- Start from latest `development`: `git checkout development && git pull && git checkout -b feature/<name>`
- Open a PR **into `development`** (squash merge preferred)
- Release: PR **`development` → `main`** only (merge commit preferred)
- Tags (`v*`) are created from `main` after that PR lands — not from a feature branch

Do not invent a different integration branch. If work is already on `main`/`development` locally, move it onto a feature branch before pushing.
